		ItemTooltip: {
			Generic: {
				HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore:
					'''
					[c/7F7F7F:Hold LEFT SHIFT for more information on this item's exact function]
					[c/7F7F7F:Hold LEFT SHIFT and LEFT CONTROL for some neat flavor text about this item]
					'''
				EdibleFromNormalUse:
					'''
					Using this item from the hotbar while holding the Eat Items keybind causes you to swallow it
					If this is a stack of multiple items, this only swallows items one at a time unless otherwise stated
					'''
				EatenByNormalUse:
					'''
					Using this item from the hotbar at all causes you to swallow it
					If this is a stack of multiple items, this only swallows items one at a time unless otherwise stated
					'''
				Broken:
					'''
					This item has been damaged too heavily for continued use and has become non-functional
					Broken items can be repaired with the Scroll of Divine Indigestion or by visiting St. Promethia
					'''

				AcidResistTier: {
					0: Does not resist any stomach acids
					1: Immune to normal stomach acids
					2: Immune to normal and enchanted stomach acids
					3: Immune to normal and enchanted stomach acids, as well as aqua regia
					99: Digesting this item requires acids blessed by the gods themselves

					100: {
						Normal: Indigestible...?
						Chronological: Indigestible...but not for you
					}
				}

				Food: {
					Short: The satisfaction of a good meal lingers longer after digesting this item
					Long: This item counts twice as much towards Well Fed tiers while digesting.
				}

				LongTooltipHelpers.SunlightExposureRules:
					'''
					[c/7F7F7F:You are considered exposed to sunlight when:]
					[c/7F7F7F:- You are above 0']
					[c/7F7F7F:- You are not in front of a background wall]
					[c/7F7F7F:- It is daytime]
					'''
			}

			Vanilla: {
				Accessories: {
					Informational: {
						REK3K: Displays number of enemies, kill and meal counts, and rare creatures
						TallyCounter:
							'''
							Displays how many enemies have been killed in the world
							Displays how many entities you've digested
							'''
					}

					Pets: {
						Light: {
							CandyFairyMasterPetItem: {
								Short:
									'''
									Summons a fairy princess to provide light and guard you from certain mobs (by eating them)
									{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
									'''
								Long:
									'''
									Summons a small prismatic fairy who calls herself the Heiress of Light. Her real name is Radianne.
									The Heiress [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:provides light in dark places].
									The Heiress [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:will hunt down and eat nearby mobs] which are shiny or twinkly enough for her tastes (including other fairies), as well as royalty.
									Her stats are as follows:
									[c/7F7F7F:> Health:] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:{MiniCandyFairyMaxHealth}]
									[c/7F7F7F:>] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:No swallow capacity limit (+ can swallow bosses)]
									[c/7F7F7F:> Stomach capacity:] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:{MiniCandyFairyStomachCapacity}]
									[c/7F7F7F:>] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Cannot be escaped]
									[c/7F7F7F:> Digestion tick damage:] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:{MiniCandyFairyDigestDamage}]
									[c/7F7F7F:> Digestion tick rate:] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:{MiniCandyFairyDigestRate}/sec]
									[c/7F7F7F:> Absorption rate:] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:{MiniCandyFairyAbsorbRate}/min]
									The Heiress [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:digests better] while a blood moon is out.
									[c/7F7F7F:> 1.5x digestion tick rate and absorption rate]
									The Heiress [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:digests much better] while the sun is out.
									[c/7F7F7F:> 2.0x digestion tick rate and absorption rate]
									The Heiress [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:digests better] while her escort is sleeping.
									[c/7F7F7F:> 1.25x digestion tick rate and absorption rate, also makes both scale with the speed of time]
									'''
								Flavor:
									'''
									The Empress always thought it very strange, the idea of having an heir to the throne in case she were rendered unfit to rule. The absolute AUDACITY of such a claim! Preposterous! She would quickly make a fool, and a fattening meal, of anyone that DARED to try and usurp her title!
									...though, as she slowly began to tutor a small prismatic fairy like herself by the name of Radianne, she began to see the value in having someone to eventually preside over, and voraciously devour the residents of, the Hallow with her. She would eat her if she tried to usurp the Empress, of course, but even a snack like her could be useful as an enforcer.

									With the Empress now dead (and/or digested), she now acts as your enforcer instead. She seeks to increase her brightness (and bulk, naturally) by devouring the brightest snacks she can swallow. Don't worry about her gut; she's eaten plenty of tough meals in the past.
									'''
							}
						}
					}

					AdhesiveBandage: {
						Short:
							'''
							Grants immunity to Bleeding
							Slightly slows Softened buildup
							Won't hold up well to a gastric assault
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							While worn by a player:
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants immunity] to [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Bleeding].
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Slows Softened buildup by {AdhesiveBandageSoftenedBuildupReduction}].
							If this item runs out of durability via indirect digestion damage, it is immediately removed from your inventory and added to the stomach contents of your predator.
							'''
						Flavor: A simple adhesive bandage, meant to halt the flow of blood from open wounds to make it easier for them to heal. Medical practitioners carry a nigh-endless number of these.
					}

					HealthRegenAndPotionCooldownBand: {
						Short:
							'''
							Slightly boosts health regeneration and lowers max potion cooldown while worn
							Boosts health regeneration more, lowers max potion cooldown, and hastens potion cooldown while digesting
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							While worn by a player:
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{HealthRegenBandIIWornHealthRegen} HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Artificial)]
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Reduces the initial duration of Potion Sickness] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:25%].
							Upon running out of durability inside a player, until fully digested, and for 10 minutes thereafter:
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{HealthRegenBandIIEatenHealthRegen} HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Artificial)]
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Reduces the initial duration of Potion Sickness] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:25%].
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Potion Sickness wears off twice as fast].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							By combining a simple rejuvenating wristband and a magical stone imbued with life essence, you've managed to make: another wristband. That does the exact same thing.
							That said, it tastes better than either of its parts! Which is always a good reason to upgrade anything, frankly. Any upgrade that makes your gear a better snack for emergencies is a good upgrade.
							'''
					}

					ShimmerCloak:
						'''
						Grants immunity to Intangibility
						Hold <down> to temporarily bypass this immunity
						Allows you to safely drink shimmer
						'''
				}

				Armor: {
					OakWood: {
						Head: {
							Short:
								'''
								Increases defense very slightly in daylight
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases defense] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:1] when [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:exposed to sunlight].
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.LongTooltipHelpers.SunlightExposureRules}
								Has no special effects when eaten.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								A makeshift helmet fashioned from oak wood.
								It has a very plain taste.
								'''
						}

						Chest: {
							Short:
								'''
								Increases defense very slightly in daylight
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases defense] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:1] when [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:exposed to sunlight].
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.LongTooltipHelpers.SunlightExposureRules}
								Has no special effects when eaten.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								A makeshift chestplate fashioned from oak wood.
								It has a very plain taste.
								'''
						}

						Legs: {
							Short:
								'''
								Increases defense very slightly in daylight
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases defense] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:1] when [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:exposed to sunlight].
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.LongTooltipHelpers.SunlightExposureRules}
								Has no special effects when eaten.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								A makeshift pair of boots fashioned from oak wood.
								They have a very plain taste.
								'''
						}

						SetBonus: {
							Short: Boosts natural health regeneration, moreso in daylight
							Long: "[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases natural health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:5%]; this is [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:doubled] when [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:exposed to sunlight]."
						}
					}
				}

				Consumables: {
					Food: {
						ChickenNugget: {
							Short:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Short}
								'Definitely contains harpy'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Long}"
							Flavor:
								'''
								Often collectively called "chicken nuggets" for simplicity's sake, these nuggets of breaded, thoroughly-cooked meat actually come from a wide variety of birds and harpies alike.
								You'll most often find these in kids' meals in fast food chains, or on the young ones' section of the menu in restaurants; more mature folks generally prefer at least full limbs of well-prepared meat, if they're not swallowing the origin bird whole and alive.
								'''
						}

						ChocolateChipCookie: {
							Short:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Short}
								'New and mmmproved'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Long}"
							Flavor:
								'''
								One of the easiest cookie types to bake.
								The chocolate chips provide an undeniably sweet and delectable tint to the firm base of a normal cookie.
								Can be easily experimented with using additional ingredients to create even more delicious cookies.
								'''
						}

						Fries: {
							Short:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Short}
								'Hey, where's the ketchup?'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Long}"
							Flavor:
								'''
								One of the most common things to do with a potato is to carve it up into nice little sticks and fry them. The result, rather uncreatively, is called a batch of fries.
								Depending on where you find these in restaurants, they can be served with a wide variety of different other foods, such as fish or burgers.
								'''
						}

						GingerbreadCookie: {
							Short:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Short}
								'No plot armor this time, fuckboy'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Long}"
							Flavor:
								'''
								The easiest type of cookie to bake. Uses no captivating ingredients whatsoever.
								In old times, an extra ingredient added to these sorts of cookies would cause them to grow sentient, fleeing from their creators. Sveetian culture still allows these cookies a place of their own (with limitations), but elsewhere? They have nowhere to run with all the sweets-hungry predators around.
								This one represents one of the simplest and least nuanced cookies to be baked with that peculiar ingredient.
								'''
						}

						PotatoChips: {
							Short:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Short}
								'Also known as crisps'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Long}"
							Flavor:
								'''
								Not quite as common a culinary choice as fries, chips are still a frequently-utilized use case for potatoes in cooking.
								Generally much crispier and crunchier than fries, which lends well to seeing them offered as snacks in places where that crunchiness is preferred.
								'''
						}

						SugarCookie: {
							Short:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Short}
								'Not made with snow, surprisingly'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.Food.Long}"
							Flavor:
								'''
								A very common treat in Sveetia due to the commonplace nature of sugar as a cooking and baking ingredient.
								Provides plenty of energy to help get through the day in batches, or a quick pick-me-up as a lone snack.
								'''
						}
					}

					Potions: {
						Ale: {
							Short:
								'''
								Makes you tipsy while, and for a minute or two after, digesting
								While tipsy, you're better with melee combat and eating people; not as good with digesting them, though
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								It's alcohol in a mug. What do you want me to say?
								Lucky you, not only are glass mugs super easy to digest, but the booze will spill over the top as it goes down your throat, too, so you'll feel the effects right away.

								While in a stomach, until fully digested, and for 1 minute and 30 seconds thereafter, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:inflicts the Tipsy debuff].
								This buff improves your melee capabilities and internal capacities, at the cost of some defense and some digestion rates.
								'''
							Flavor: A simple glass of ale. Most drunkands would swallow mugs like these by the pound with ale still in them, or even drink the kegs dry directly. Sometimes, they'd even swallow down the kegs themselves!
						}

						Sake: {
							Short:
								'''
								Makes you tipsy while, and for a short while after, digesting
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								It's alcohol, but fancy! And in a fancy bottle!
								Since you're just swallowing the whole bottle, with the cap still on, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
								As such, it may take a moment before you really start to feel the good vibes you're drinking this stuff for.

								Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 3 minutes thereafter, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:inflicts the Tipsy debuff].
								This buff improves your melee capabilities and internal capacities, at the cost of some defense and some digestion rates.
								'''
							Flavor: A well-made beverage from the heart of Turea, made predominantly for its endless lineages of princes and princesses...yet still marketed as a drink for the wealthy of other countries, and an exotic booze for those with a few currencies to spare.
						}

						Regeneration: {
							Short:
								'''
								Helps regenerate health while digesting
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Improves your body's ability to heal itself from injuries when drank.
								Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
								You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

								Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 6 minutes thereafter:
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{RegenPotionRegenFlat} HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Artificial)]
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								Simple beginner-level potions like this one are as commonplace as any other tech these days, being meant to help adventurers keep on their feet and off their fellows' waistlines.
								This one's in an easy-to-swallow bottle, and meant to help gradually patch up smaller injuries. Unfortunately for you, it probably won't save you from being churned up alive.
								'''
						}

						Wrath: {
							Short:
								'''
								Boosts damage and your ability to quiet down your prey while digesting
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Improves the damage output of your swings, shots, and stomach alike when drank.
								Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
								You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

								Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 3 minutes thereafter:
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{WrathPotionDamageBoost}].
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{WrathPotionTUMBoost}].
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases ACI] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{WrathPotionACIBoost}].
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								An amateur-level potion fashioned from the oils of a spiteful fish which makes its home in pitch-dark purple Corrupted waters.
								While digesting, it makes the consumer rather angry, increasing their combat and predatory prowesses alike. An adventurer with this would-be curse could easily carve up and churn down their fellows into a healthy layer of fat just as easily as they could their foes.
								'''
						}

						Rage: {
							Short:
								'''
								Boosts crit chance and your ability to swallow new prey and finish churning old ones while digesting
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Improves your precision with your attacks and makes you better at getting down live prey and sloshing dead ones into cellulite when drank.
								Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
								You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

								Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 3 minutes thereafter:
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases critical strike chance] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{RagePotionCritChanceBoost}].
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases GLP] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{RagePotionGLPBoost}].
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases ABS] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{RagePotionABSBoost}].
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								An amateur-level potion fashioned from a bloody subspecies of piranha which makes its home in the sanguine seas of the Crimson.
								While digesting, it makes the consumer uncannily accurate with their shots and stomach, targeting weak points while shooting up, swallowing down, and sloshing all around (what's left of) their prey, regardless of whether that prey was once an ally or not.
								'''
						}
					}

					LifeCrystal: {
						Short:
							'''
							On use, the crystal is broken apart, providing a few revitalizing effects
							These effects also apply when it is eaten, and eating it provides additional bonuses
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							When eaten by anything:
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Heals for {LifeCrystalEatHeal} health] instantly upon running out of durability.
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Regeneration buff] while digesting; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{LifeCrystalEatRegenLength} seconds] once fully digested.
							When used normally by a player OR upon running out of durability when eaten by a player:
							- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:increases maximum health] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:20].
							- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:increase TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:1].
							  - The above two bonuses can stack for up to {LifeCrystalsMax} crystals used/eaten.
							- If you have reached 15 Life Crystals used/eaten, permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:mitigates the impact of stomach weight] by {MaxLifeCrystalsPermaWeightReduction}x.
							Life Crystals used/eaten by this character (max. {LifeCrystalsMax}): [c/{LifeCrystalsUsedColor}:{LifeCrystalsUsed}].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A mysterious crystal which forms in the deeper caverns of Terraria, drawing in all manner of adventurers, curious and craving alike, to examine it. Upon breaking one apart, either via pure force or prolonged exposure to a gastric gauntlet of digestion, the crystal fires off a spell which lends its power to the user/consumer, greatly increasing their vitality...though part of the effect only occurs up to a certain number of times. The exact science behind this spell is poorly understood, but has led many to believe a powerful being created these crystals with the intention of letting them be eaten by worldly creatures in need of strength to hunt. While this was initially thought to be an unfounded claim, the fact that powerful predators have caught truly unnaturally perfect prey in the past suggests otherwise...
							Those who have eaten Life Crystals before note that doing so feels a lot like eating rock candy, with a notable cherry-like flavor. The first person to do it ended up famous worldwide for quite some time because of a number of hilariously inept, yet somehow successful achievements. A pity he ended up getting gulped down and gurgled by a gleeful, gluttonous ghost.
							'''
					}

					LifeFruit: {
						Short:
							'''
							Provides a swathe of truly revitalizing effects when eaten
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							When eaten by anything:
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Heals for {LifeFruitEatHeal} health] instantly upon running out of durability.
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Regeneration buff] while digesting; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{LifeFruitEatRegenLength} seconds] once fully digested.
							When eaten by a player who has eaten at least 15 Life Crystals, upon running out of durability:
							- Permanently [c/{LifeFruitHealthBonusColor}:increases maximum health by 5].
							- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:increases TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{LifeFruitStomachStrengthBonus}].
							- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:increases ACI] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{LifeFruitAcidStrengthBonus}].
							  - The above three bonuses can stack up to {LifeFruitMax} times.
							Life Fruit eaten by this character (max. {LifeFruitMax}): [c/{LifeFruitUsedColor}:{LifeFruitUsed}].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A mysterious crop only ever found in the depths of a specific jungle on Terraria, this delectable fruit seems like only a rare delicacy at first...but when sufficient residual mana sourced from Life Crystals' magic swirls within the body of the consumer, it bestows upon them and their stomach greater power than a Life Crystal ever could. Many have speculated these were coerced into growing in much the same way that Life Crystals are thought to have been...and given that angels from a plane beyond have documentedly visited our planet and even been eaten by particularly ambitious predators on it, this isn't such an outlandish claim.
							While rather few have managed to taste the fruit in full, due to a certain trio of feminine floral demis deep in the jungle craving them and those who would seek out their craved snacks at all times, those who have managed to gulp down these fruits have reported a pleasant and tasteful combination of orange and mango flavors as the main appeal of the Life Fruit as an exotic snack option.
							'''
					}

					ManaCrystal: {
						Short:
							'''
							On use, the crystal is broken apart, providing a few magically beneficial effects
							These effects also apply when it is eaten, and eating it provides additional bonuses
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							When eaten by anything:
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ManaHeal}:Restores 100 mana] instantly upon running out of durability.
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Mana Regeneration buff] while digesting; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{ManaCrystalEatManaRegenLength} seconds] once fully digested.
							When used normally by a player OR upon running out of durability when eaten by a player:
							- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ManaHeal}:increases maximum mana] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:20].
							- Permanently [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:increases the ABS stat] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:1].
							  - The above two bonuses can stack for up to {ManaCrystalsMax} crystals used/eaten.
							Mana Crystals used/eaten by this character (max. {ManaCrystalsMax}): [c/{ManaCrystalsUsedColor}:{ManaCrystalsUsed}].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							Very commonly made and just as commonly munched on, these oversized star-shaped batches of blue-raspberry-flavored rock candy are infused with residual mana from pieces of the stars above, making them readily provide those who eat them with additional space in their mana reserves and an easier time processing meals that have fallen still into more mana for said reserves.
							Many have speculated that there could be less eating-oriented approaches to using these, but why would you care about that when you can munch on such a big batch of blue-raspberry-flavored rock candy?

							...and then someone proved why it could be a bad idea to overspecialize, so now the spell also fires off if the rock candy is broken apart.
							'''
					}
				}

				Currency: {
					Coins: {
						Generic: {
							Short: Can be used in shops
							Long:
								'''
								Coins in your inventory will [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:auto-convert to highest denominations] whenever possible.
								Can be used as currency in most shops.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								of a currency long since abandoned by most countries.
								However, those who travel the space between those countries still find it useful to use it for trades with people who live in the wilder regions of Terraria.
								'''
						}

						CopperCoin: {
							Short:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Short}
								'Not made of chocolate, sadly'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Used as the lowest denomination of "universal" currency.
								100 of these have equal value to a [i:SilverCoin] Silver Coin.
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Long}
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								The lowest denomination {$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Flavor}
								These are often treated as little more than individual bites of cereal in most areas, these are often doomed in massive amounts to the gut of anything, and anyone, that wants to churn them into gut fat.
								Roughly equal in value to:
								- Avarsici: Favor.
								- Sveetia: [c/FFAFAF:Too low value.]
								- Turea: N/A.
								- Desperais: N/A.
								'''
						}

						SilverCoin: {
							Short:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Short}
								'Also not made of chocolate, also sadly'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Used as the second-lowest denomination of "universal" currency.
								1 of these has equal value to 100 [i:CopperCoin] Copper Coins.
								100 of these have equal value to 1 [i:GoldCoin] Gold Coin.
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Long}
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								The second-lowest denomination {$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Flavor}
								Snacking on these is fairly common against those who can make a comfortable living elsewise, though you won't find those with lower-paying jobs doing so...very much.
								Roughly equal in value to:
								- Avarsici: 1 Mark.
								- Sveetia: [c/FFAFAF:Too low value for conversion.]
								- Turea: N/A.
								- Desperais: N/A.
								'''
						}

						GoldCoin: {
							Short:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Short}
								'Voted 'Most Likely To Be Made Of Chocolate'!...but it isn't'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Used as the second-highest denomination of "universal" currency.
								1 of these has equal value to 100 [i:SilverCoin] Silver Coins.
								100 of these have equal value to 1 [i:PlatinumCoin] Platinum Coin.
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Long}
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								The second-highest denomination {$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Flavor}
								Snacking on these usually means you're fairly wealthy, being able to doom at your leisure small swathes of your riches to a fate even better than your bank account: bulking up your backside.
								Roughly equal in value to:
								- Avarsici: 1 Great Mark.
								- Sveetia: 4 Sugar Sterlings.
								- Turea: N/A.
								- Desperais: N/A.
								'''
						}

						PlatinumCoin: {
							Short:
								'''
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Short}
								'Still need to know if it's made of chocolate? Are you just that eager to gurgle all your wealth into a wealth of belly fat?'

								'...because it's not made of chocolate'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Used as the second-highest denomination of "universal" currency.
								1 of these has equal value to 100 [i:GoldCoin] Gold Coins.
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Long}
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								The highest denomination {$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Vanilla.Currency.Coins.Generic.Flavor}
								Snacking on these generally denotes someone of extremely high value --- such high value that even the best denomination of currency is naught but pleasant cereal to them.
								Alternatively, some lower-class may swallow individual coins of this caliber for the experience --- there is a certain exotic rush that comes with swallowing something worth a small fortune like a mere snack, digesting it into naught but a few more calories or a bit of belly fat, and having the only evidence it was ever there be a pleasant little belch that rises from your belly.
								Roughly equal in value to:
								- Avarsici: 1 Grand Mark.
								- Sveetia: 400 Sugar Sterlings.
								- Turea: N/A. Turean folk trade in material (or living) possessions, not petty currency.
								- Desperais: N/A. People pay, and charge, in good, meaty, fighty food around those parts.
								'''
						}
					}
				}

				Placeables: {
					Gems: {
						Amber: {
							Short:
								'''
								A very sweet-tasting "gem"
								'Pretty sappy, if you ask me'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Can be found sometimes within the desert, either on its own or when extracted from [i:3347] Desert Fossils.
								Can be used to fashion a select assortment of desert-related items.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								Many people in old times assumed this was a gemstone. It's not! It's actually fossilized tree sap which found a home in desert regions, nestling in the remains of creatures from ages past.
								While it IS possible to create amber through fairly simple means, most of these means have subsequently been heavily commercialized and privatized by the desserts industry. Why? It's simple!

								Amber tastes very sweet. Sweet-tasting things are desserts to be enjoyed! And where there are desserts to be enjoyed...there's ALWAYS money to be made.
								'''
						}

						Amethyst: {
							Short:
								'''
								A rather common gemstone
								'Conducts mischief, predominantly'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Found fairly commonly in the caves of the world.
								Can be used to fashion assorted early-game items.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								A common gemstone such as amethyst can be found in virtually any cave that travels subsurface, though the purple hues of this one give off a certain...vibe.
								Amethysts are most typically used as conduits for the abilities of shapeshifters to be more easily controlled, amongst other mischievous use cases.
								'''
						}

						Diamond: {
							Short:
								'''
								A valuable, rare gemstone
								'Chromatic diversity is so last setting'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Found rarely in the deeper (accessible) layers of the world.
								Highly valuable, or at least used to be. Could sell for a lot of money.
								Can be used to fashion assorted powerful early-game items.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								Oftentimes mistakenly assumed to be the hardest gem in existence, formed in the deep layers of Terraria's crust as the result of ages of time and temperament. However, in more recent times, alongside the view of a natural set of four as an omen from worlds beyond being proven false, even tougher gems have been found and even forged with modern life's own means.
								While technology --- both magical and electrical entwined --- has advanced enough to create these gems decently reliably, naturally-formed diamonds are still a valuable commodity, as artificially-compressed diamonds carry traces of other materials and thus have substantially lower purity.
								Swallowing one isn't recommended, as it is by far the toughest gem to digest due to its sheer hardness...but if you can, having a large enough diamond for dinner is said to make your body much sturdier, inside and out.
								'''
						}

						Emerald: {
							Short:
								'''
								A fairly valuable and rare gem
								'Conducts...focus? Is focus a quantifiable metric?'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Found fairly rarely in the deeper (accessible) layers of the world.
								Valuable. Could sell for a decent amount of money.
								Can be used to fashion assorted accuracy-boosting early-game items.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								A fairly rare gemstone colored a precise, hungering green.
								Emeralds are gemstones often attributed to the likes of ranged weapon enthusiasts, its shine when held to light almost resembling the predatory glint in a storied archer's eye when they spot their latest prey.
								Swallowing one often isn't recommended due to its hardness, but if you can, having a large enough emerald for dinner is said to improve your eyesight, and thus, your accuracy for the shots and snacks  that matter.
								'''
						}

						Ruby: {
							Short:
								'''
								A fairly valuable and rare gem
								'Conducts heat'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Found rarely in the deeper (accessible) layers of the world.
								Highly valuable, or at least used to be. Could sell for a lot of money.
								Can be used to fashion assorted strength-boosting early-game items.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								A fairly rare gemstone colored a pleasantly warm red.
								Rubies are very common gems to find in any gear suited to a brawler, as they're often said to represent the fire inside of the fighter's heart (and stomach).
								Swallowing one often isn't recommended due to its hardness, but if you can, having a large enough ruby for dinner is said to make you and your stomach pack a bigger punch.
								'''
						}

						Sapphire: {
							Short:
								'''
								A fairly valuable and rare gem
								'Conducts mana'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Found rarely in the deeper (accessible) layers of the world.
								Highly valuable, or at least used to be. Could sell for a lot of money.
								Can be used to fashion assorted magical early-game items.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								A fairly rare gemstone, colored a pleasantly dark blue.
								Sapphires are very common gems to find in any gear suited to a mage or adjacent, as they tend to conduct mana the best out of all gemstones.
								Swallowing one often isn't recommended due to its hardness, but if you can, having a large enough sapphire for dinner is said to make you smarter.
								'''
						}

						Topaz: {
							Short:
								'''
								A rather common gemstone
								'The lamest of them, too'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Found very commonly in caves that travel beneath the surface.
								Can be used to fashion assorted (not very powerful) early-game items.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								Easily one of the most common and, not coincidentally, most lame gemstones ever discovered on Terraria.
								Can make for a good snack in a pinch, though it can be tough to digest without a strong system.
								'''
						}
					}
				}

				Weapons: {
					Melee: {
						BorealWoodSword: {
							Short:
								'''
								Can be swung to deal damage
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long: "[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Left-click] to swing the sword, dealing [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DealDamage}:100% damage] to struck targets."
							Flavor: A simple sword fashioned from boreal wood. Has a chilly aftertaste resembling the taste of snow.
						}

						CactusSword: {
							Short:
								'''
								Hurts your throat a noteworthy bit to swallow
								While digesting, enemies that hit you take damage themselves
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								When eaten:
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:Deals {CactusSwordSwallowDamage} damage to the pred] when swallowed.
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:Inflicts {$Mods.V2.StatusEffects.Voraria.Debuffs.SoreThroat.Name} for {CactusSwordSoreThroatTime} seconds] when swallowed.
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Thorns buff] while digesting, and for [c/FFFF7F:{CactusSwordThornsTime} seconds] longer once fully digested.
								'''
							Flavor: A dubiously-wieldy sword fashioned from cactus cuttings. While its prickly nature makes it fairly usable as a weapon, one has to wonder how it would taste...and if there's any way to get around the discomforting amount of spines it still has.
						}

						FruitcakeChakram: {
							Short:
								'''
								Throw it to get it as far away from yourself as possible; alternatively, you can eat it
								No matter how angry eating it makes you, it is unfortunately the best way to rid the world of this menace
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								When eaten:
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:Deals {FruitcakeChakramSwallowDamage} damage to the pred] when swallowed, because it just tastes that bad.
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:Inflicts {$Mods.V2.StatusEffects.Voraria.Debuffs.SoreThroat.Name} for {FruitcakeChakramSoreThroatTime} seconds] when swallowed; see above
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:Inflicts the Poison debuff] while in your stomach, and for [c/FFFF7F:{FruitcakeChakramPoisonTime} seconds] longer once fully digested; see above.
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Wrath buff] while in your stomach, and for [c/FFFF7F:{FruitcakeChakramWrathTime} seconds] longer once fully digested, because needing to eat this thing makes one VERY angry.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								A single look at this abominable crime against catering makes you wonder if it was ever supposed to be food in the first place. The mere THOUGHT of gracing this...THING with death by digestion almost seems too good a mercy for it.

								You're not alone in that assessment, either. Fruitcake was first made long ago by a rather...eccentric baker in a territory previously owned by one of the many, MANY royals that have made their mark on Terraria over the years.

								It is now banned within any and all Avarsician borders; the very kingdom whose then-prince Markus Caldera originally annexed the country (and its queen) as a way to prove his worth (and, to his credit, he WAS successful on both fronts) as heir to the throne.
								The Apex Convocation unanimously agreed to ban it from Desperais, and despite the hundreds of years and countless shifts in the seat fillings that have passed since that initial ruling, that ban has never been lifted.
								Countless other territories outside of these two notable powers also ban it, and only ever for one reason: the mere existence of this concept is slander against the good name of bakers the planet over.

								The only use this has is as a weapon, and POTENTIALLY as emergency rations if all else is gone.
								'''
						}

						OakWoodSword: {
							Short:
								'''
								Can be swung to deal damage
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long: "[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Left-click] to swing the sword, dealing [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DealDamage}:100% damage] to struck targets."
							Flavor: A simple sword fashioned from oak wood, and tasting about the same.
						}
					}

					Ranged: {
						BorealWoodBow: {
							Short:
								'''
								Can fire arrows to deal damageF
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Left-click] to shoot an arrow, dealing [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DealDamage}:100% damage] to the first target it hits.
								Some arrows may have [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:special properties]; examine these in the tooltips of your arrows.
								'''
							Flavor: A simple bow fashioned from boreal wood. Has a chilly aftertaste resembling the taste of snow.
						}

						OakWoodBow: {
							Short:
								'''
								Can fire arrows to deal damage
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Left-click] to shoot an arrow, dealing [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DealDamage}:100% damage] to the first target it hits.
								Some arrows may have [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:special properties]; examine these in the tooltips of your arrows.
								'''
							Flavor: A simple bow fashioned from oak wood, and tasting about the same.
						}
					}
				}

				Feather: {
					Short:
						'''
						'Don't pluck me! They went thataway!'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Can be used to craft certain wing types.
						Can be used as a potion ingredient.
						'''
					Flavor:
						'''
						A simple feather plucked from the wing of a hungry harpy.
						These feathers are often arranged in fashions that promote easy targeted flight, allowing the greedy birds in the sky to swoop down and scoop up their kicky, shouty prey with ease.
						'''
				}

				Gel: {
					Short:
						'''
						Was a part of a gelatinous creature. It's bouncy!
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
						'''
					Long:
						'''
						Gel is used by the gelatinous creatures in the Terrarian world. 
						If this piece of gel is alive or not is not easy to determine, but you can swallow it with ease. Quite tasty too.
						'''
					Flavor: Tastes similar to sweet jelly, and closer to a berry - similar to Blueberries!
				}
			}

			Voraria: {
				Armor: {
					CloverArmorSetBonus: 7 defense, drastically increased struggling strength

					CloverHeadAccessories: {
						Short:
							'''
							7% increased critical strike chance
							Increased maximum prey swallowing size and struggling strength
							Slightly increased luck
							'Three head accessories in one slot? Is that even legal?'
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases critical strike chance] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:7%].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases luck] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:0.3].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases GLP] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:5].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases struggle strength] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:75%].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							Clover's choice of headwear. It is an amalgamation of items stuffed into a single slot.
							It consists of:
							- A four-leaf clover hair... hatpin?
							- An awfully bright tophat
							- 'Felt Goggles', despite not actually being made of felt.
							At first, Clover didn't actually like green that much, but eventually it grew on her.
							'''
					}

					CloverSweater: {
						Short:
							'''
							7% increased critical strike chance
							Increased struggle strength
							Increased stomach capacity, struggling strength and food absorption rate
							Slightly increased luck
							'It's awfully comfortable. You could probably fall asleep standing just by wearing this...'
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases critical strike chance] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:7%].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases luck] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:0.1].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:8].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases ABS] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:6].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases struggle strength] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:100%].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							One of Clover's many sweaters. It is pretty large for both you and her.
							It is RIDICULOUS how soft and comfortable this thing is.
							You'd think it's like, enchanted or somethi- OH WAIT it is.
							'''
					}

					CloverStockings: {
						Short:
							'''
							7% increased critical strike chance
							20% increased movement speed
							Increased struggling strength
							Lowers stomach weight
							Slightly increased luck
							'They're more like thigh high socks, honestly.'
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases critical strike chance] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:7%].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases luck] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:0.1].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases movement speed] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:20%].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:15%].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases struggle strength] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:75%].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							It's a pair of Clover's stockings!
							...uh, what do you want me to say about this
							they're just enchanted socks
							like
							dude
							'''
					}
				}

				CheatItems: {
					RoseFlower: {
						Short:
							'''
							Gives you the same predatory prowess that Rose has, at no cost whatsoever
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							While worn, provides a number of extremely- and outright unfairly-beneficial predatorily-centric effects:
							[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Makes your stomach weightless, no matter what or who is in it.]
							[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Grants infinite swallow and stomach capacity, and makes it impossible for prey to escape your stomach unless you regurgitate them.]
							[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Grants the ability to eat bosses regardless of whether your currently-selected gear and abilities would allow you to.]
							[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Raises your acid tier to MILES beyond the maximum.]
							[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases digestion tick rate by a factor of 4.]
							[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases absorption rate by a factor of 8.]
							Several item effects and UI elements will be modified while this item or any of its counterparts are equipped.
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:this is a prefabricated copy of Rose's personal hairpin]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:it's not where any of her more                egregious predatory abilities come from]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:she is naturally just that much a glutton. ate an entire mountain range once]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:she tells people that this flower was the very last thing left from the last world she ate]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:she doesn't tell them that I made it for her when I made her]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:I made a virtually-infinite number of 'em so that if she accidentally ate it]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:(and she has, multiple times)]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:she'd have another rarin' to go shortly thereafter to keep her happy]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:she tells me these flowers are delicious]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:then again, she thinks everything's delicious, so maybe take her word with a grain of salt]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:don't try to eat it]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:she'll know]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:and she'll make you a meal, no matter how strong you are or how invincible you think you are]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:after all, she REALLY likes the taste of these flowers]
							'''
					}

					VenomDevItem: {
						Short:
							'''
							Gives you the same predatory digestive prowess that Venomizeous has, at no cost whatsoever
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							While worn, provides a number of extremely- and outright unfairly-beneficial predatorily-centric effects:
							[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Makes your stomach weightless, no matter what or who is in it.]
							[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Grants infinite swallow and stomach capacity, and makes it impossible for prey to escape your stomach unless you regurgitate them.]
							[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Grants the ability to eat bosses regardless of whether your currently-selected gear and abilities would allow you to.]
							[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Raises your acid tier to MILES beyond the maximum.]
							[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases digestion tick rate by a factor of 4.]
							[c/7F7F7F:> ][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases absorption rate by a factor of 8.]
							Several item effects and UI elements will be modified while this item or any of its counterparts are equipped.
							'''
						Flavor: "[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.VenomCommentary}:Test]"
					}

					SecondBestAngelFeather: {
						Short:
							'''
							Gives you St. Promethia's blessing to cram yourself into anyone you please
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long: "[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Allows you to get eaten by (be it naturally or by climbing into) anything that is able to eat people, even if it couldn't fit you otherwise.]"
						Flavor:
							'''
							A single feather from the one and only St. Promethia Hypate, an angelic gut slut who'd love nothing more than to see herself melted down into flab for every last predator on the planet and off of it --- even those that one would assume are unable to eat her.
							This is one of her favorite feathers, churned down into padding endless times, yet still as fresh as the day she was born. Simply holding it makes you feel like you haven't seen nearly enough of the greediest predators of the world.
							'''
					}

					ServerMessageRelay: {
						Short:
							'''
							Allows a certain someone to speak directly into your world
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long: When kept in Rose's inventory, allows the [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:/authormessage] command to work.
						Flavor: "[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ThomasCommentary}:hi :>]"
					}
				}

				Accessories: {
					Informational: {
						MealSizeScanner: {
							Short:
								'''
								Shows the size of nearby snacks, and helps you know if you're able to make them your next meals
								Functions from the inventory as well as normal accessory slots
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Most things that you can eat [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:display their size as a meal above themselves].
								If their size number is [c/00FF00:green], you are able to swallow them with ease.
								[c/7F7F7F:This means that your target meal would fit in your stomach normally, and nothing is keeping you from gobbling them up on sight. Go indulge a little!]
								If their size number is [c/FFFF00:yellow], you are able to swallow them, but might have a bit of trouble keeping them down or properly mulching them.
								[c/7F7F7F:This means that while your target meal would fit in your stomach normally, one of the following is true:]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your stomach is too full to fit them due to other meals already inside it]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your target meal's defense exceeds your stomach's digestion tick damage]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your target meal's health exceeds 1 minute of your stomach's final DDPS (digestion damage per second, factors in defense)]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your target meal's acid resist level exceeds your stomach's acid tier]
								If their size number is [c/FF0000:red], you aren't able to gulp and gurgle them into gut fat yet.
								[c/7F7F7F:This means that your target meal wouldn't fit in you due to your throat and/or stomach capacity being too low.]
								[c/7F7F7F:If this is the case, try to increase your GLP and TUM stats by whatever means you find throughout the game!]
								Functions from the inventory as well as when equipped in normal accessory slots.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								This peculiar device was originally designed for use by a mechanic to ensure optimal fullness-to-caloric-value weighting when consuming nearby living creatures and converting them into (potential) energy.
								It can do the same for you, if you care to, though its main use will almost certainly be making sure your eyes don't get bigger than your stomach...and/or throat.
								'''
						}

						PredCapacityScanner: {
							Short:
								'''
								Shows the stomach capacity of nearby entities that can eat you, and lets you know if you're able to take some time off in their gut
								Functions from the inventory as well as normal accessory slots
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Most things that can eat you [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:display their stomach capacity as predators below themselves].
								If their capacity number is [c/00FF00:green], they're able to swallow you with ease.
								[c/7F7F7F:This means that your choice predator could fit you in their stomach normally, and nothing is keeping them from gobbling you up on sight. Ready to get gurgled?]
								If their capacity number is [c/FFFF00:yellow], they're able to swallow you, but might have a bit of trouble keeping you down or properly mulching you.
								[c/7F7F7F:This means that while your target pred could fit you in their stomach normally, one of the following is true:]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Their stomach is too full to fit you due to other meals already inside it]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your defense exceeds their digestion tick damage]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your health exceeds 20 seconds of their stomach's final DDPS (digestion damage per second, factors in defense)]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your acid resist level exceeds your desired predator's stomach's acid tier]
								If their capacity number is [c/FF0000:red], they aren't able to gulp and gurgle you into gut fat.
								[c/7F7F7F:This means that your target predator isn't able to eat you, since their stomach won't be able to hold you. A sad day, indeed.]
								Functions from the inventory as well as when equipped in normal accessory slots.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								Exposing an electronics implement to shimmer, most times, doesn't actually short-circuit it like water or stomach acid might, but instead tends to warp the implement's functionality to a new use case similar to, yet also very different, its initial purpose.
								This almost otherworldy-looking device performs a similar task to its non-shimmered counterpart, but analyzes the digestive capacity of scanned subjects instead. While this is useful for anyone looking to get mulched by a nice, hungry tummy, it's not particularly useful to a predator in comparison to its normal form.
								'''
						}
					}

					Vanity: {
						BalloonBelly: {
							Short:
								'''
								Can be blown up or deflated, and wrapped around your tummy to make it look bigger!
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Can be worn in any vanity accessory slot to make your stomach always appear larger proportional to the size of the balloon.
								Current size is {InflatedSize}; maximum size is {MaximumInflatedSize}.
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Left-click] to inflate the balloon if it is not at its max size, increasing its size by 1.
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Right-click] to deflate the balloon if it has air in it, decreasing its size by 1.
								Does nothing when equipped in a non-vanity accessory slot.
								'''
							Flavor: This funny-looking balloon is pre-fitted with a waistband for easy attachment to...well, specifically the stomach. Blow it up enough, and it'll replicate all the great looks of a massive, meat-filled gut without any of the downsides, complete with color-changing latex exterior so you get just the matching color you and your tummy want! Just note that it won't make all the happy gurgling and groaning a REAL bellyful of squirmy snacks makes.
						}
					}

					AntiDigestionSash: {
						Short:
							'''
							Decreases taken digestion damage and slows Softened buildup slightly
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Decreases taken digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{AntiDigestionSashDigestionDefenseBonus}].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Slows Softened buildup] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{AntiDigestionSashSoftenedBuildupReduction}].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A simple sash made out of leathers, feathers, and silk, often hastily put together and worn by less confident adventurers.
							While it won't hold up to a continued gastric assault, it can help stave off the acids of a hungry tummy in a pinch.
							'''
					}

					NymphHairScarf: {
						Short:
							'''
							Increases movement speed and lowers stomach weight
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases movement speed] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{NymphScarfMoveSpeedBuff}].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{NymphScarfWeightReduction}].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A pleasantly comfortable scarf sewn with the luscious locks of at least one or two delicious, deceitful damsels found throughout Terraria's great caverns.
							Sewn into the scarf are sapphires and miniature runes which allow the wearer to be lighter on their feet, even (or perhaps, especially) with a good gutful of meat (still alive or otherwise) slowing them down, mimicking the stomach-centric swiftness of a hungry nymph.
							'''
					}

					PromethiaAntiDigestionSash: {
						Short:
							'''
							Decreases taken digestion damage and slows Softened buildup substantially
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Decreases taken digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PromethiaAntiDigestionSashDigestionDefenseBonus}].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Slows Softened buildup] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PromethiaAntiDigestionSashSoftenedBuildupReduction}].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A sparkly, tasty-looking sash made of a material similar to gold, yet possessing the consistency of silk...as well as some actual divine-looking silk, this sash is standard-issue equipment for lower-ranking Sinhunters from the heavens beyond.
							It holds up against greedier gastric assaults much better than its mortally-designed counterpart, and is designed to grant eaten angels some time to properly teach their predator just how low said predator still is on the greater food chain.
							St. Promethia, of course, keeps hers with her not because she wants to get out of the predators that snack on her, but rather, because she wants just a little more time to...enjoy herself, for lack of a better term, inside those hungry tummies.
							'''
					}
				}

				Charms: {
					BetterDigestion: {
						Short:
							'''
							Makes your acids a little bit stronger
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long: "[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases ACI] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{AcidStrengthBonus}]."
						Flavor: A beginner-level charm designed to make the bearer's stomach acids substantially more potent than if they were to go without it. Very useful for first-time predators who could really use that extra kick to their digestive juices to secure their first few big meals, though sadly not particularly worthwhile past those starting stages.
					}

					Fatass: {
						Short:
							'''
							Lets you take on much bigger prey...but at what cost?
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Doubles] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:swallow and stomach capacities].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Halves] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:digestion damage and tick rate].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A high-risk, high-reward charm typically only offered to skilled adventurers with a greedy enough tummy to negate its downside; it is often plucked from these adventurers by nymphs as one of the few things that can survive the gastric torment of such deceitful ladies' gluttonous tummies.
							While worn, it redirects a part of the muscle and nerve firings from actively digesting swallowed prey, instead putting that bodily power towards stretching the throat and stomach to gobble up and gorge oneself on ever-larger prey. It's not hard to see why nymphs see them as a valuable trinket, as would anyone else.
							'''
					}

					LessStomachWeight: {
						Short:
							'''
							Makes your stomach lighter, but only if you're not too full
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{WeightReduction}].
							If your stomach is at {FullnessEffectivenessLossThreshold} fullness or more, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:this effect becomes less effective the less capacity you have to spare.]
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A rather strange charm, almost mechanical in nature, purpose-built to make one's stomach significantly less of a burden to lug around while it's filled to capacity with sufficiently satisfying caloric fuel.
							While it works in most cases, it does this by passively generating a layer of helium inside of the bearer's stomach; thus, if there isn't sufficient room to provide said helium deposits, the charm becomes significantly less effective, to the point of eventually doing nothing if there is no space to add helium.
							'''
					}

					PreyItemTheft: {
						Short:
							'''
							May cause you to belch up certain items from your meals
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Upon dying to digestion,] prey you eat [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:have a chance to drop certain items].
							Some items dropped this way will be [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:unique] to these tables, while others will be [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:existing drops] from the prey (with [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:lower/limited drop rates]).
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A very simple charm.
							The only noteworthy thing about it is the big, shiny...tasty coin...perfectly...in the center...

							...donning it makes you feel incredibly...hungry. Hungry for valuables. Maybe your future meals would be kind enough to give you some so you don't end up snacking on your tasty new charm?
							'''
					}

					RegenFromAbsorption: {
						Short:
							'''
							Grants health and mana regeneration while digesting dead prey
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							While digesting dead prey, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:based on how much you absorb in a minute:]
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{HealthRegenerationRatio} of absorption rate in HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Natural)]
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ManaHeal}:Increases mana regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{ManaRegenerationRatio} of absorption rate in MP/sec].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Effectiveness decreases if there are prey in your stomach still alive.]

							Current regeneration ({RegenEffectiveness} effectiveness with {LivePreyRemaining} out of {PreyRemaining} prey still alive):
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:{CurrentHealthRegen} HP/sec]
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ManaHeal}:{CurrentManaRegen} mana/sec]
							'''
						Flavor: An intermediate-level charm designed to ease the long-standing issue of one's digestive system granting surprisingly little reprieve from the heat of battle. As long as a surplus of food resides in the bearer's stomach, this charm will convert some of the excess calories into mana to fuel a spell which revitalizes the bearer both physically and magically. Of course, this spell can only work as quickly as the bearer's belly can digest its meals.
					}
				}

				Consumables: {
					Catchables: {
						Pinky: {
							Short:
								'''
								When used, a delicious little Pinky is released into the world
								Hold the Swallow key while using this item to instantly gulp down the released Pinky
								Has a very pleasantly sweet taste, granting a few buffs when eaten
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								When eaten by anything:
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Heals for {PinkyEatHeal} health] instantly upon running out of health.
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Happy! buff] while in a stomach; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{PinkyEatHappyLength} seconds] once fully digested.
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Regeneration buff] while digesting; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{PinkyEatRegenLength} seconds] once fully digested.
								May have any number of positive consequences if given to someone as a sweet treat of a gift.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								With how diverse slimes are in size, shape, and savor, it's no surprise that some slimes end up hunted almost exclusively for their beloved flavor. No slime embodies this more directly than the Pinky, a very small slime which is HIGHLY prized for the following traits:
								1) Its bite-size nature, allowing even the smallest and most inexperienced of predators to swallow it with relative ease.
								2) Its lovely flavor, which much resembles cotton candy, though almost all are uncertain as to where this sweet flavoring actually originated.
								3) Its vibrant pink coloration, from which it gets its name.
								'''
						}
					}

					PermanentUpgrades: {
						Jujus: {
							BlankJuju: {
								Short:
									'''
									Can be crafted into juju accessories that can provide stat boosts
									{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
									'''
								Long: This item does nothing on its own; instead it is used to craft a variety of stat boosting accessories, that can additionally be digested for a minor permanent boost.
								Flavor:
									'''
									One of Clover's strange creations.
									It is a fragment of magical energy, waiting for the right conditions to be awakened.
									'''
							}

							ShimmerJuju: {
								Short:
									'''
									Increases maximum prey swallowing size, stomach capacity, acid strength and food absorption rate
									If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to this juju's effects
									{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
									'''
								Long:
									'''
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases GLP, TUM, ACI & ABS] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{All}].
									When eaten:
									- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Permanently increases GLP, TUM, ACI & ABS] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PermAll}].
									This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:will have no further effect].
									'''
								Flavor: '''[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.CloverQuote}:"The Aether? The shimmer lake is sooo cooool! I bet it tastes like candy!" -Clover]'''
							}

							BiomeJujuForest: {
								Short:
									'''
									Increases stomach capacity and food absorption rate
									If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to this juju's effects
									{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
									'''
								Long:
									'''
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{TUM}].
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases ABS] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{ABS}].
									When eaten:
									- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Permanently increases TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PermTUM}].
									- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Permanently increases ABS] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PermABS}].
									This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:will have no further effect].
									'''
								Flavor: '''[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.CloverQuote}:"The forest? Hmm, layin' around in the grass with a tum full of candy is always fun!" -Clover]'''
							}

							BiomeJujuDesert: {
								Short:
									'''
									Increases acid strength and struggling strength
									If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to this juju's effects
									{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
									'''
								Long:
									'''
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases ACI] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{ACI}].
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases struggle strength] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{STR}%].
									When eaten:
									- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Permanently increases ACI] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PermACI}].
									- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Permanently increases struggle strength] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PermSTR}%].
									This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:will have no further effect].
									'''
								Flavor: '''[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.CloverQuote}:"The desert? Ugh, it feels awful with the constant heat! Never going there!" -Clover]'''
							}

							BiomeJujuSnow: {
								Short:
									'''
									Increases maximum prey swallowing size and food absorption rate
									If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to this juju's effects
									{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
									'''
								Long:
									'''
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases GLP] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{GLP}].
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases ABS] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{ABS}].
									When eaten:
									- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Permanently increases GLP] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PermGLP}].
									- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Permanently increases ABS] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PermABS}].
									This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:will have no further effect].
									'''
								Flavor: '''[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.CloverQuote}:"The tundra? Not a fan of ice, but the snow makes me think of ice cream!" -Clover]'''
							}

							BiomeJujuJungle: {
								Short:
									'''
									Increases stomach capacity
									Decreases movement speed
									If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to this juju's effects
									{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
									'''
								Long:
									'''
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{TUM}].
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:Decreases movement speed] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{SPD}%].
									When eaten:
									- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Permanently increases TUM] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PermTUM}].
									This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:will have no further effect].
									'''
								Flavor:
									'''
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.CloverQuote}:"The jungle? Reminds me of the time where I drank like three gallons]
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.CloverQuote}:of honey and then got all sticky... Took a while to crawl out of the hive." -Clover]
									'''
							}

							BiomeJujuSky: {
								Short:
									'''
									Decreases stomach weight
									Increases movement speed & jump height
									If eaten for the first time, permanently gain slight buffs related to this juju's effects
									{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
									'''
								Long:
									'''
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{WeightReduce}%].
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases movement speed] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{SPD}%].
									[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases jump speed] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{Jump}%].
									When eaten:
									- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Permanently decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PermWeightReduce}%].
									This bonus only applies once. Eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:will have no further effect].
									'''
								Flavor: '''[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.CloverQuote}:"The sky? The lower gravity up there makes my tum feel all kinds of funny..." -Clover]'''
							}
						}

						PureSwallowBoost1: {
							Short:
								'''
								Permanently increases the strength of your throat when used or eaten
								Can only be used once; further uses and/or consumptions do nothing special
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Using or eating this item] will permanently grant you the following bonus:
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases GLP] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PureSwallow1GLPBonus}].
								This bonus only applies once. Using or eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:will have no further effect].
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								One of the first physical stimulants for predators ever created was a drug to enhance the potential of the throat, allowing for easier swallowing of anything, and anyone, that the recipient wanted packed into their gut.
								This stimulant has been replicated countless times, and is now standard-fare as an entry-level predatory aid across the world of Terraria.
								'''
						}
					}

					Potions: {
						FastDigestionPotion: {
							Short:
								'''
								Speeds up digestion while digesting
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Induces a variety of predatorily-centric effects when drank, almost all involving digestive power.
								Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
								You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

								Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 1 minute thereafter:
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:+{FastDigestionPotionACIBonus} ACI]
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:+{FastDigestionPotionABSBonus} ABS]
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Raises acid tier to 3][c/7F7F7F:, if it is not at 3 already]
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								Digestive aids are commonplace in medical establishments across Terraria to help with particularly rowdy or troublesome prey, with just about every option that entails available for use to make sure your system doesn't get backed up with all the parts of your prey you can't quite melt down (yet).
								This is a rather simple variant carried by medical practitioners at all times (be they for your use or theirs). Dropping something small into the bottle seems to cause it to be swiftly dissolved by the mysterious substance within...not that it's much of a surprise, really. Even inanimate objects can be ravenously hungry --- enough to eat a person, in the right circumstance. People just always seem to make great meals...

								...well, that snack in your stomach won't wait much longer. Bon appetit!
								'''
						}

						StomachCapacityPotion: {
							Short:
								'''
								Allows your stomach to hold a bit more than usual while digesting
								'For when you're craving an extra snack or two for dessert'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Improves your stomach's holding capacity when drank.
								Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
								You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

								Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 3 minutes thereafter:
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:+{StomachCapacityPotionCapacityBonus} stomach capacity]
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								A commonplace and easily-brewable predatory enhancer in the Terrarian world, this potion uses a simple mix of relaxing agents, mainly found in fish, to allow a predator's stomach to stretch a good bit past its normal limits.
								Sadly, though, it won't bolster your stomach's durability against internal fighting at all; you'd best hope you can keep down all that extra meat you'll be able to fit into your hungry tummy.
								'''
						}

						StomachacheMeterCapacityPotion: {
							Short:
								'''
								Improves your stomach's resistance to the struggles of your prey while digesting
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								Improves your stomach's ability to keep prey from causing a ruckus inside you when drank.
								Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
								You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

								Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 3 minutes thereafter:
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases stomachache meter capacity] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{StomachacheMeterCapacityPotionMeterCapacityBonus}].
								> The struggles of your prey will deal [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:-{StomachacheMeterCapacityPotionUneaseDefenseBonus} less struggle damage].
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								One of a number of common brews made for predatory types, this potion is often sold by medical practitioners to those who need that one particularly feisty femme or burly breakfast they had to settle down and digest, ideally without hacking them back up.
								It makes use of several well-known gastric relaxants to ease the stomach and throat, lowering the amount that unruly prey can kick up a stomachache and heightening the amount they'd need to do so in order to induce vomiting.
								'''
						}
					}

					SpecialItemUpgrades: {
						PaperMaidSummon: {
							RawStats: {
								Short:
									'''
									{PaperMaidName} might like this item
									{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
									'''
								Long:
									'''
									This item can be fed to {PaperMaidName}, the paper maid summoned by the [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{$Mods.V2.ItemName.Voraria.Weapons.Summon.PaperMaidSummon}], by right-clicking on her with it.
									Once she fully digests this item, {PaperMaidName} will permanently gain automagic self-lamination, conferring the following buffs:
									> +{LaminatedHealth} health.
									> +{LaminatedStomachCapacity} stomach capacity.
									> +{LaminatedStomachacheMeterCapacity} stomachache meter capacity.
									> +{LaminatedDigestionRatio} digestion damage ratio.
									'''
								Flavor:
									'''
									This small device, a marvel of magical conduction cross-bred with machine lamination, is designed to be able to laminate anything and everything simply by placing the desired item inside it and waiting.
									Early prototypes erroneously proved capable of accepting people as input and laminating. These prototypes have since been stored in their creator's personal stash for later testing and revision.
									That said, while lamination is often used as a tool to hunt origami creations in the wild, fallen off trading caravans and originally left over from Sveetia's annual Sugar Crane Festival, it is also used by the Sveetian people to reinforce their greatest works.
									'''
							}

							Flight: {
								Short:
									'''
									{PaperMaidName} might like this item
									{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
									'''
								Long:
									'''
									This item can be fed to {PaperMaidName}, the paper maid summoned by the [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{$Mods.V2.ItemName.Voraria.Weapons.Summon.PaperMaidSummon}], by right-clicking on her with it.
									Once she fully digests this item, {PaperMaidName} will permanently gain paper crane wings, conferring the following buffs:
									> Gains flight capabilities, and will fly as her master or target does.
									> Increased accuracy and range for dash attack ([c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:RIGHT-RIGHT-RIGHT] instruction).
									'''
								Flavor:
									'''
									A poor, damaged origami crane, worn down by evading the ever-growing hunger of the average office worker for a nice, well-laminated snack from Sveetia while on lunch break.
									While its wings are battered and its flight rendered all but gone, it still has strength to give...but not to those who would hunt it for a light meal.
									No, this weak, dying crane searches for another of its kin, another Sveetian origami piece, to give itself wholly to...

									...lending, to that creation, the great power of flight.
									'''
							}
						}
					}

					DigestionRepairScroll: {
						Short:
							'''
							Using this item will instantly relieve you of most of the downsides of predator or preything lifestyles
							After it is used, a full day must pass before it can be used again
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							This item can only be used once at least one full day has passed since the last time it was used.
							Upon usage, it will instantly:
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Fully repair all items in your inventory] that have taken digestion damage and can be repaired.
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Remove all Softened stacks still applied to you] from any lingering acid burns from recent encounters.
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Clear all indigestion-related debuffs you may have] from particularly troublesome meals.
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							It's a scroll, inscribed with countless runes that you've never seen before; notably, they look surprisingly similar to, yet so very different from, musical notes...which would help, if the scroll bothered to say anything about the actual composition of the piece. Whoever wrote this sheet music didn't think it through very well from the perspective of one who might want to play it.
							In any event, incomprehensible as it may be at a cursory glance, as you go to look at it closer, the runes fade into the background somewhat, and a second layer of text fades in which is actually comprehensible to the average person:

							[c/FF3FBF:CHORUS (sing in D# major):]
							[c/FF3FBF:From heavens inward and a cauldron outward, the Conductress' graces shall smile.]
							[c/FF3FBF:By Melodia's song, this verse, when not wrong, shall save from a fate all too vile.]

							[c/FF3FBF:I near face the Veil, the edge of our great hail, as a chance predator's left me weak,]
							[c/FF3FBF:So by Melodia's song, I sing a chorus along, for my strength to return to its peak.]

							[c/7F1F5F:POST-CHORUS (composer's note):]
							[c/7F1F5F:But the song must rest, asleep in its nest, 'fore its strength can remend its own peak,]
							[c/7F1F5F:So by my sacred song, don't dare sing this wrong; I've no care for the melodically weak.]

							...you can't help but wonder if Promethia stole this from someone.
							'''
					}

					DigestionUpgradeTablets: {
						Short:
							'''
							Can only be eaten once you've fully gained the stomach-strengthening effects of Life Fruit and enchanted your stomach acids beforehand
							Permanently modifies your digestive system using a delayed-effect bioalteration spell once fully digested
							This mixes nitric acid into the structure of your stomach acid, turning it into aqua regia (royal water)
							This change makes your stomach significantly better at digesting things, and allows you to digest more things you wouldn't normally be able to
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							This item can only be eaten once you have eaten and digested at least {LifeCrystalsMax} Life Crystals, at least {ManaCrystalsMax} Mana Crystals, and at least {LifeFruitMax} Life Fruits.
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Permanently grants +40 ACI.]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Permanently grants +20 ABS.]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Raises your acid tier to Royal (2).]
							This upgrade is permanent, but only takes effect once the pack is fully digested.
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							Despite how often these things were flaunted around as the future of predatory prowess and a marvel of modern magical bioengineering back in the day, the real marvel is that these somehow pose no significant health risks despite mixing an entire secondary acid into an already-powerful stomach. The label on the side suggests eating the entire pack...including the pack itself. The pack supposedly has much better nutritional value than the pills, so...bottoms up.
							Obtaining more than one pack of these tablets is prohibited by Avarsician law and punishable by...well, predominantly fucking about and learning what for. It's not exactly hard to guess why a spell that assumes you haven't taken the pills at all is bad if you've already melted down a full pack of them before.
							'''
					}

					FeatherDuster: {
						Short:
							'''
							Can only be used in a hungry tummy
							Can be used to tickle and/or agitate your predator's stomach a lot; often enough for them to belch you back up
							'Now taken very literally'
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							Can only be used while inside something's stomach.
							When used, instantly [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:deals] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{FeatherDusterStruggleDamage}] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:struggle damage] to your predator.
							If this would fill up their stomachache meter, it instead caps at its usual maximum, and you are [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:instantly belched out].
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							Often carried around by the bundle by harpies, the core purpose of this feathery broom-like implement is to agitate the stomach of hungry predators, forcing them to belch and/or cough up whatever (and WHOever) they ate alongside the user.
							More modern uses for evolved forms of this implement include maids' cleaning work, on-the-job snacks for said maids, impromptu microphones-turned-mini-meals on budget karaoke nights, and mitigating a wide array of magical incantations.
							'''
					}

					HairDyeCapacity: {
						Short:
							'''
							Changes the color of your hair based on how full you are
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Changes the color of your hair] based on [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:how full your stomach currently is].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:When your stomach is empty], makes your hair a dark red.
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:When your stomach is completely full], makes your hair a pleasantly full green.
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A special hair dye, purpose-mixed for the fashionable predator in your life (be it yourself or someone else).
							On a full stomach, this dye gives off a stunningly pleasant green, while the dark red one's hair will turn while running on empty is just as attractive. A number of other colors end up in the spotlight if the wearer's stomach isn't 100% full, but still has some meat in it, and all of them are specially designed to make one's hair as appealing as possible.
							After all, how can your prey resist ending up a part of those luscious locks if you've got just the right color to make them weak in the knees?

							DISCLAIMER: Excess calories from digested meals may not actually increase hair length.
							'''
					}

					SteampunkerGutFastTravel: {
						Short:
							'''
							Can only be used in a hungry tummy?
							Can be used to save yourself from impending digestion into ass fat, probably?
							'The latest and greatest in instantaneous transportation!...or so she says.'
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							Can only be used while the Steampunker is alive.
							When used, instantly [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:teleports you] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:out of your current predator's stomach], if applicable...[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:and into the Steampunker's].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Does not work] while in the Steampunker's stomach.
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							A peculiar little trinket fashioned together by the Steampunker, the great lass she is, for a measly sum.
							It can be used anywhere as a one-way teleport, even workable in the most gluttonous guts to instantly get you out of digestive jeopardy...but to what catch?
							Much to the Steampunker's frustration, though, it doesn't yet work across planes of reality, nor from excessively long distances. She's still working on that functionality.
							'''
					}

					DemonCandy: {
						Short:
							'''
							Provides regeneration when digested
							'Isn't this just a jawbreaker covered in chocolate?'
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							'''
						Long:
							'''
							When eaten:
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Regeneration buff] after running out of durability; this lingers for [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{Regen} minutes].
							If dropped onto the ground in the Underworld, it might bait out certain types of monsters.
							'''
						Flavor:
							'''
							It is, infact, a jawbreaker covered in chocolate.
							Appears to be the favourite food of a certain type of monster in the lava-filled depths of the Underworld.
							'''
					}
				}

				Weapons: {
					Ranged: {
						Throwables: {
							FragileBottles: {
								Generic: {
									Short:
										'''
										Can be thrown to coat a target in {ThrowableBottleLowercaseCondimentName}
										Coated targets may attract the appetites of certain predators
										Will damage friendly entities
										'''
									Long:
										'''
										[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Left-click] to throw a bottle of {ThrowableBottleLowercaseCondimentName}.
										The bottle [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DealDamage}:deals 100% damage] to the first entity it hits, shattering instantly.
										Struck enemies are [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:coated in {ThrowableBottleLowercaseCondimentName}] for 20 seconds.
										'''
									Flavor: For virtually as long as humanoids have existed on Terraria, they have tried to find numerous ways to coat their prey, living and otherwise, in delicious substances to enhance their flavor. A popular pick amongst modern-day brawlers is these throwable bottles, shattering on impact and coating prey in whatever they contain.
								}

								Honey: {
									Short: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Weapons.Ranged.Throwables.FragileBottles.Generic.Short}"
									Long:
										'''
										{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Weapons.Ranged.Throwables.FragileBottles.Generic.Long}
										Honey-coated snacks will attract the attention of predators that like [c/FF7FBF:sweet] flavors.
										'''
									Flavor:
										'''
										{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Weapons.Ranged.Throwables.FragileBottles.Generic.Flavor}
										This bottle contains a healthy helping of sweet, delicious honey, sourced from the genuinely obscenely large bee hives scattered about Terrarian jungles. A single sip enlightens the tongue with a sugary-sweet flavor that, while by far beaten out by Sveetian sugar and its resultant papercrafts, still brings happiness to the mind. Any predator with a sweet tooth is sure to come a-hunting prey coated in this stuff.
										'''
								}

								HotSauce: {
									Short: "{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Weapons.Ranged.Throwables.FragileBottles.Generic.Short}"
									Long:
										'''
										{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Weapons.Ranged.Throwables.FragileBottles.Generic.Long}
										Hot sauce-coated snacks will attract the attention of predators that like [c/FF7F00:spicy] flavors.
										'''
									Flavor:
										'''
										{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Voraria.Weapons.Ranged.Throwables.FragileBottles.Generic.Flavor}
										This bottle contains a healthy helping of dangerously-hot Luke's Lightweight Lava(tm), a brand of hot sauce based in Desperais which Lucinda and countless other demons buy in bulk on the regular. A single sip trials the tongue with a scorching-hot sensation akin to drinking lava straight out of the lake...just without any of the gastrointestinal death that comes with unprotected lava drinking. Any predator craving some spice in their diet is bound to come running for prey coated in this stuff.
										'''
								}
							}
						}
					}

					Summon: {
						PaperMaidSummon: {
							Short:
								'''
								[c/FF0000:This item is not currently functional, and will not be until beta 5]
								[c/FF0000:This tooltip acts as a preview of its intended functionality]
								Summons a capable maid(...?) to fight for you
								She requires {NeededMinionSlots} minion slots available to be summoned, and has no sisters
								Can throw paper plates and simple silverware at enemies, as well as eat them or you
								Prey she eats get papercuts as they digest
								If eaten, she gives internal papercuts to her predator (intentionally or not) until sufficiently digested
								'Maidche to serve'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								[c/FF0000:This item is not currently functional, and will not be until beta 5]
								[c/FF0000:This tooltip acts as a preview of its intended functionality]
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Left-click] to summon a maid to your cursor position. Her name is {Name}!
								{Name} requires {NeededMinionSlots} minion slots available to be summoned. There can only be one of her at once.
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Left-click] again while summoned and no instructions are being performed to teleport {Name} to your position.
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Right-click] to select the closest entity to the cursor for targeting. From here, you can command {Name} by inputting specific click combinations:
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:RIGHT-LEFT-LEFT] to have {Name} throw a paper plate at the target, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DealDamage}:dealing {PaperPlateDamage} damage].
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:RIGHT-LEFT-RIGHT] to have {Name} throw a set of paper mache silverware at the target, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DealDamage}:dealing 3x{SilverwarePerDamage} damage].
								> The fork [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DealDamage}:ignores up to {ForkArmorPen} defense].
								> The spoon [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DealDamage}:deals {SpoonInorganicDamageBonusPercent} higher damage to inorganics].
								> The knife [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DealDamage}:inflicts Bleeding on applicable enemies for {KnifeBleedTime} seconds].
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:RIGHT-RIGHT-LEFT] to have {Name} swing a broom at the target if close enough, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DealDamage}:dealing {BroomDamage} damage].
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:RIGHT-RIGHT-RIGHT] to have {Name} dash towards the target. If she contacts the target in this state, she immediately snatches them into her mouth, swallowing them in short order.
								{Name}'s stomach has a [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:capacity of {StomachCapacity}] and a [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:stomachache meter capacity of {StomachacheMeterCapacity}].
								{Name}'s stomach [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:deals {DigestionDamage} digestion damage {DigestionRate} times per second].
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:{DigestionBleedRatio} of digestion damage] is instead [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DealDamage}:converted to a Bleeding proc which persists even if prey escape] her stomach.
								If eaten by anything, {Name} has {Health} health, and [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DealDamage}:passively inflicts Bleeding on her predator] until she dies from digestion.
								If eaten by you, {Name} [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:will not struggle in your stomach].
								If you feed yourself to {Name}, her stomach will not digest you unless you ask to be digested.
								While in {Name}'s stomach:
								> She will not eat any other prey, even if they try to weasel their way into her mouth, unless you are already being digested.
								> The [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:RIGHT-RIGHT-RIGHT] input can be performed inside {Name}'s stomach to [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:instruct her to digest you].
								> All damage dealt to her is redirected to her stomachache meter.
								> If her stomachache meter fills, you and any other contained still-alive prey will be forcefully ejected.
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								Magical implements used by adventurers that have since lost their lives to the gluttony of the undergrowth are often twisted by wherever they happen to get got. This poor thing's owner must have perished in a cave full of mushrooms.
								Notably, the fairies that stay around these preferred regions seemed to like implements like these a lot; if you were to shake this about, perhaps one would come to your aid and shield you from oncoming fire (with, of course, their greedy tummy).
								'''
						}

						ShroomFairySummon: {
							Short:
								'''
								Summons fungal fairies to protect you from long-range attacks by swallowing them up
								'A bunch of fun gals, really'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								'''
							Long:
								'''
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Left-click] to summon a fungal fairy to your cursor position.
								Each fungal fairy requires 1.5 minion slots available to be summoned.
								While active, fungal fairies will [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:dash over to and devour hostile projectiles] that stray too close to you.
								If they become too full of tasty enemy ranged attacks, they'll have to take a moment to rest and digest before they can actively gobble up more.
								As they gain weight, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:they'll digest faster and be able to hold more in their tums], [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:at the cost of moving slightly slower].
								While digesting, fungal fairies [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:release healing spores] that [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:heal for 5 health upon contact, or 10 if you swallow them].
								'''
							Flavor:
								'''
								Magical implements used by adventurers that have since lost their lives to the gluttony of the undergrowth are often twisted by wherever they happen to get got. This poor thing's owner must have perished in a cave full of mushrooms.
								Notably, the fairies that stay around these preferred regions seemed to like implements like these a lot; if you were to shake this about, perhaps one would come to your aid and shield you from oncoming fire (with, of course, their greedy tummy).
								'''
						}
					}
				}

				NymphHairStrand: {
					Short:
						'''
						Used to make Sky Blue Dye
						'Thieved from a deceitful, yet delicious damsel'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
						'''
					Long: Can only be obtained by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:eating and digesting a Nymph with the Charm of the Thief equipped].
					Flavor: A lock of a nymph's succulent silvery-blue hair, somehow spared from the gastric gauntlet of a gut such as yours. One could make a potent dye or a comfortable scarf out of this. A hair stylist would also quite like something as unique as this...
				}

				ObserverPupil: {
					Short:
						'''
						'Now i've seen everything.'
						{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
						'''
					Long: Obtained by killing an Observer. They can be found in the sky.
					Flavor: A large pupil. That's all there really is to say on the matter.
				}
			}
		}

		Projectiles: {
			DisplayName: {
				Vanilla: {
					Summons: {
						Pets: {
							FairyPrincess: Heiress of Light
							MiniIceQueen: Ice Princess
						}
					}
				}
			}

			ShroomFairy.DisplayName: Fungal Fairy
			ShroomFairySpore.DisplayName: Fairy Spore
			CLOVERPUNCH.DisplayName: C L O V E R P U N C H
		}

		InfoDisplayName.TallyCounterVore: Meal Count
		InfoDisplayText.TallyCounterVore.InvalidMeal: Meal count unavailable

		StatusEffects: {
			Vanilla: {
				Buffs: {
					Campfire.Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{CampfireRegenFlat} HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Natural)]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases base natural regeneration buildup speed] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{CampfireNaturalRegenBuildupSpeed}].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases digestion tick rate and absorption rate] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{CampfireDigestionSpeedBonus}].
						'Everything's better with a nice, warm fire nearby'
						'''
					HeartLantern.Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{HeartLanternRegenFlat} HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Artificial)]
						'You feel a bit more lively than usual'
						'''
					Honey.Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{HoneyRegenFlat} HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Natural)]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases the speed at which natural regeneration builds up] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{HoneyNaturalRegenBuildupSpeed}].
						'Savor the sweet, delicious taste of good health!'
						'''
					Rage.Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases critical strike chance] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{RageCritChanceBonus}].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases throat strength (GLP)] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{RageGLPBonus}].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases absorption strength (ABS)] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{RageABSBonus}].
						'You and your stomach feel a rush of pointed fury'
						'''
					RapidHealing.Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{RapidHealingRegenFlat}]. [c/7F7F7F:(Artificial)]
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases the speed at which natural regeneration builds up] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{RapidHealingNaturalRegenBuildupSpeed}].
						'''
					Regeneration.Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{RegenPotionRegenFlat} HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Artificial)]
						'You feel slightly revitalized'
						'''
					Wrath.Description:
						'''
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{WrathDamageBonus}].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases stomach strength (TUM)] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{WrathTUMBonus}].
						[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases acid strength (ACI)] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{WrathACIBonus}].
						'You and your stomach feel a rush of raw fury'
						'''
				}

				Debuffs.Tipsy.Description:
					'''
					[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases melee damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{TipsyMeleeDamageBonus}].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases melee critical strike chance] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{TipsyMeleeCritChanceBonus}].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases melee attack speed] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{TipsyMeleeAttackSpeedBonus}].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:Decreases defense] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{TipsyDefenseCut}].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases fishing skill] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{TipsyFishPowerBonus}].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases swallow and stomach capacities] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{TipsyCapacityBonus}].
					[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:Decreases digestion tick rate and absorption rate] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{TipsyChurnRateCut}].
					'''
				Summons.Pets.FairyPrincess.Description:
					'''
					A small, but very hungry prismatic fairy [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:follows you around].
					She will [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:hunt down and eat nearby entities] which are shiny or twinkly enough for her tastes (including other fairies), as well as royalty.
					'The light of the fair folk illuminates all (especially her next lunch)'
					'''
			}

			Voraria: {
				Buffs: {
					CharmofMythsChurnBuff: {
						Name: Healthy Snack: Charm of Myths
						Description:
							'''
							You've opted to add a Charm of Myths to your waistline, conferring the following buffs until it's done setlling down on your hips:
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{CharmofMythsChurnRegen} HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Artificial)]
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Reduces the initial duration of Potion Sickness] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:25%].
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Potion Sickness wears off twice as fast].
							'The only myth left to bust about it now is whether it'll add to your booty or belly. Place your bets!'
							'''
					}

					FastDigestionPotionBuff: {
						Name: Digestive Aid
						Description:
							'''
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases acid strength (ACI)] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{FastDigestionPotionACIBonus}].
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases absorption strength (ABS)] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{FastDigestionPotionABSBonus}].
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases your acid tier] to 3 if it is not there already.
							'Maybe now your stomach can solve that little blockage for you...'
							'''
					}

					StomachCapacityPotionBuff: {
						Name: Elasticity
						Description:
							'''
							> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases your maximum stomach capacity] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{StomachCapacityPotionCapacityBonus}].
							'Now go and have a little dessert! You've earned it.'
							'''
					}

					StomachacheMeterCapacityPotionBuff: {
						Name: Internal Endurance
						Description:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases your maximum stomach unease by {StomachacheMeterCapacityPotionMeterCapacityBonus}.]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Decreases the amount of unease generated by struggling prey by {StomachacheMeterCapacityPotionUneaseDefenseBonus}.]
							'That should keep your squirmier snacks down a bit better!'
							'''
					}
				}

				Debuffs: {
					MoltenStomach: {
						Name: Molten Stomach
						Description:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Your stomach is getting melted from the inside by the lava you drank.]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Maybe don't drink lava without a way to prevent this outcome.]
							'do you are have stupid'
							'''
					}

